    "llmlang.cli.load_config": {
      "file": "llmlang/cli.py",
      "text": "+ loads the [tool.llmlang] table from pyproject.toml, degrading gracefully when it can't be read\naccepts a starting directory and an optional explicit config path override\nloads the [tool.llmlang] table from pyproject.toml, degrading gracefully when it can't be read\nuses the override path directly when given, otherwise finds the nearest pyproject.toml from the starting directory\nwarns to stderr and returns an empty config, rather than crashing, when the override path doesn't exist or when this Python has no tomllib (needs 3.11+)\nreturns an empty config when no pyproject.toml is found at all\nreturns the [tool.llmlang] table",
