    "llmlang.cli.run_check": {
      "file": "llmlang/cli.py",
      "text": "+ checks every path given, applying config-resolved coverage and exclusions, and reports every failure together\naccepts a list of file or directory paths, the parsed flags, an optional config path override, and the output format\nchecks every path given, applying config-resolved coverage and exclusions, and reports every failure together\naccepts any number of file or directory paths, auto-discovering every *.llm file under a directory and checking a .llm file directly\nwarns to stderr and skips a path that doesn't exist, rather than failing the whole run\nexits with an error if no .llm files are found under any given path\nprints \"checking X\" progress and any warnings to stderr, so stdout stays clean for the report in either format\nexits 0 if every checked file was clean, 1 otherwise",
      "text_hash": "abc8a57646f8242cba719f6610569a55b6bfc7f99d30dec108b5e6361c00f3ab",
      "code_hash": "b9ddca013f67caa8582c768a4cb5db37069e3792041a245943b71e9e10ebfeb3",
